# Test projects a change makes compile: programs the compiler refused before
# the change and builds after it (a program it built and ran wrong goes in
# tests/started-passing).  One per line, the project's directory name under
# tests/tests/projects, then the reason:
#
#     chain_default_param_conflict a generic parameter's type is its declaration's
#
# `make verify ARGS="--baseline REV"` applies the lines this file carries and
# REV's copy does not.  For each it asserts that REV's compiler refuses the
# project with an error diagnostic, that the compiler under test builds it, and
# that the baseline's test census fails on exactly these projects.  Their
# objects are left out of the comparison: the baseline's are only what it
# compiled before refusing (dependencies, typically), so there is no program
# on its side to compare against.  A line stays once committed: against a
# later baseline it is inert, against an earlier one it is asserted again.
generic_receiver_by_type a method whose receiver is written as one instantiation of its generic owner is specialized for the owner instantiations that are that type, compared as types: one written for B's `Point` is no longer specialized for A's (E0204 at a field only B's has), and one written for `Wrapper<i32>` or `Wrapper<Box2<i32>>` exists on it (E0358 before)
generic_function_type_argument a function type returning a pointer or an array is a generic argument like any other; its printed text ending in `*` or `[]` made it a pointer or an array, an unresolvable instantiation (E0900)
generic_function_named_like_type a generic function or static method sharing its name with a type is specialized with every name in its signature and body that resolves to the type still meaning the type; the name's spelling matched the template's and was rewritten to the function's specialization (E0200 "expected 'Tag', found 'Tag<i32>'")
supertrait_methods_through_bound a supertrait is a trait reference as a bound writes one, so `type trait Ranked : cmp::Ord` names `Ord` through its module, where the parser took a bare identifier only and the program was a cascade of E0100 parse errors
path_call_generic_method a generic method called through a path with its receiver first, `Q::go(&q, 7)` or `(BetaG for NgTf)::go(&g, 7)`, binds its own type parameters and runs its specialization, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0636, or LLVM "Incorrect number of arguments") or the path took another specialization's return type (E0200)
bound_call_through_index_field_projection a call a generic body writes on a bounded parameter reached through an index (`this.ptr[i].equals(value)`), a field of an instantiation (`node.key.equals(key)`) or a projection (`value.compare(&best)` under `where This::Item: Ord`) names the bound's method, where it was re-selected by name and refused (E0156 `equals`/`compare` is both an inherent method of `Q` and provided by a trait) for a type with both
bound_path_names_declaring_trait a path through a bounded parameter, `T::make()`, names the member of the bound whose trait or supertrait declares it (`where T: Beta + Named`, `where T: Sub` with `Sub : Gamma`), where only a parameter with exactly one bound was directed, to that bound's own trait, and both were refused at the instantiation (E0156 "`make` is provided by more than one trait implemented for `P`")
impl_qualified_path_in_generic_method a path naming a trait implementation's generic method on a concrete type, `(Bb for S)::go(&this.s, w)`, written inside a generic body with the body's own type parameter as an argument, runs that method's specialization for each instantiation, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0636 "codegen: cannot resolve 'S::go'")
trait_method_through_field_in_generic_body a trait implementation's generic method called on a concrete receiver reached through a field, `this.s.go(w)` or `t.s.go(w)`, inside a generic body runs its specialization for each instantiation, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0900 "LLVM reports: Incorrect number of arguments passed to called function!")
import_type_and_function_same_leaf a type and a function of one leaf imported from two modules bind in their own namespaces; the second import was recorded as a tie with the first whatever their namespaces (E0154 at every use, E0231 at the call)
import_alias_binds_same_item an import entry takes `as` and binds its declaration under the alias, and `import A::B as C;` names the item `B` of `A` when no module is `A::B`; a brace import of an overloaded function binds every overload (it was E0243 at the one entry), where the brace alias was a parse error (E0100) and the single form E0500
import_module_alias_resolves a whole-module alias binds the module's identity, so `J::twice(3)`, `J::Tag::make(3)`, `J::Kind::B` and the rest resolve in the aliased module, where `import A::B as C;` with no module `A` was E0500 at discovery and every use of a one-segment alias was E0233, E0203 or E0201
export_alias_offers_item an `export` entry takes `as` and offers its binding to importers, and `export M as F;` offers the module, where the entry alias was a parse error (E0100)
overload_qualified_call_selects a module-qualified call to an overloaded function calls the signature its arguments select, through the path, a module alias and an export alias, where the path pinned the whole family and codegen refused it (E0900 "names several functions and the call was not pinned", E0636)
method_value_takes_receiver_first a method with a receiver named by path is a function value taking the receiver first, where the path was typed as its owner and a call through it was E0202 (`cannot find function `f``) and an annotated binding E0200
drop_in_place_releases_by_destructor an `intrinsic function` takes generic parameters, and `drop_in_place::<T>(p)` releases `*p` through `T`'s destructor found by identity, then its fields' glue, where the declaration was a parse error (E0100 "expected '('")
generic_intrinsic_from_another_module a generic intrinsic declared in another module is called through that module, and `drop_in_place::<T>(&place)` is lowered like a pointer argument, where the call was refused as private (E0353 "`..::Rel::drop_in_place` is private") and a `&place` argument reached the linker unlowered
generic_body_call_keeps_written_answer a call written in a generic type's method keeps the answer it got where it is written in every specialization, bound to the receiver's copy by identity, where the specialization of `Bx<T>::run` for `Bx<i32>` selected `this.m()` again by name and was refused (E0156 "`m` is both an inherent method of `Bx<i32>` and provided by a trait implemented for it")
trait_at_two_arguments_selects_by_argument a type implementing one trait at two trait arguments binds, for a call through the trait, the implementation whose method its argument fits, where the second implementation was refused as an internal error (E0900 "`mul` was selected by name as a trait's method, and the method table of the implementation the trait and the receiver select answers a different one")
generic_method_overloads_select_by_arguments two generic methods sharing a name at different arities are each instantiated for the calls their arguments select, where the two-argument call was instantiated from the one-argument declaration and refused (E0900 "LLVM module verification failed ... Incorrect number of arguments passed to called function!")
enum_ctor_unminted_argument a generic enum constructor with no expected type infers its instantiation from an argument that is an instantiation not yet minted (`String<GlobalAlloc>` before monomorphization); it kept the generic base, and `const o = Option::Some(String::from_string("hi"))` was refused (E0200 "expected `Option`, found `Option<String<GlobalAlloc>>`")
generic_type_and_function_share_path a generic type and a generic function written under one path are two definitions, and the template registry holds one template for each; registered by their path, the function's replaced the type's, which then had no field (E0204 "no field or method `v` on type `Main::Wrap`")
implicit_converter_free_function an `![implicit]` free function converts the argument it is registered for, by a call bound to its definition, where the call was built from its name and refused (E0214 "mismatched types")
implicit_converter_on_another_type an `![implicit]` static method declared on one type and returning another converts through the type that declares it, where the call was made on the type it returns and refused (E0233 "cannot find `Meters::to_feet`")
generic_function_overloads_select_by_arity two generic functions overloading a name by arity are each instantiated for the calls their argument count selects, inferred or turbofished, where a call to the overload the name's stamp did not name was refused (E0214 "no overload of `pick` accepts these arguments", and E0200 for `pick::<i32>(8, 9)`)
generic_owner_path_returns_parameter a generic owner's method returning its bare parameter or a pointer to it, called through a path writing the owner's arguments (`Box2::<i32>::get(&bx)`), is typed with those arguments substituted, where the return stayed `T` and the binding it initialized was refused (E0200 "mismatched types", twice)
closure_argument_to_two_overloads one capturing closure passed to two overloads of a free function is specialized once for each, kept under the overload it was made from, where the specialization was kept under the family's path and the second call was handed the first overload's and refused (E0214 "no overload of `pick` accepts these arguments")
static_match_arm_narrows_param an arm of a `static match (T)` listing several types calls a method of each listed type on a `T` value (`u8 | i32 => { x.clamp(0 as T, 50 as T) }`), checked and copied once per listed type, where the arm was checked with `T` abstract and refused (E0358 "no method named `clamp` found on type `T`")
generic_bare_name_infers_in_own_body a generic type's bare name inside its own body infers its arguments from the call (`Pair::make(x, x)` in `Pair<T>::twin<U>` makes a `Pair<U>`), and `This::` names the enclosing type with its own parameters, where `This::` was refused (E0203 "cannot find type `This` in this scope") and the bare name was collapsed to the enclosing `Pair<T>` in every copy (E0214 "expected `i32`, found `i64`")
generic_operator_on_user_type an operator on a type parameter its bound licenses (`a + b` under `T: Add<T, T>`, `a == b` under `Eq`, `a < b` under `Ord`) is desugared to the trait's method on the generic body and kept in each copy whose parameter is a user type, where `a < b` in the `V2` copy was left with an unbound `is_lt` (E0900 "internal: call to `is_lt` ... reached codegen with no resolved method")
qualified_overload_returns_selected_signature a call through a module path to an overloaded function (`Conv::conv(5 as i32)` beside `conv(f64) -> f64` and `conv(i64) -> i64`) has the return of the overload its arguments select in the type check after monomorphization too, where that check typed it with the return of the overload registered last (E0200 "mismatched types ... expected `i32`, found `i64`")
generic_reference_operator_on_user_type a comparison whose left operand is a reference to a type parameter its bound licenses (`a == b` with `a: &T` under `T: Eq`, `a < b` under `Ord`) is desugared to the trait's method on the generic body and kept in each copy whose parameter is a user type, where `a < b` and `a >= b` in the `V2` copy were left with an unbound `is_lt` / `is_ge` (E0900 "internal: call to `is_lt` ... reached codegen with no resolved method")
overloaded_function_value_by_expected_type an overloaded function taken as a value is the overload the expected function type selects - a binding's annotation, a function-typed parameter, a return type, for `Conv::conv` and a free `twice` alike - where the first overload was taken whatever the expected type, and every binding of another overload was E0200/E0214 (ruling 135)
call_through_computed_function_value a call whose callee is a function value an expression computes (`pick()(2.0)`, `maker()(10)` returning a struct) has the function's return type and is called through the value, where the type check gave the call the callee's own type (E0200 "expected `f64`, found `(f64) -> f64`") and code generation crashed asking the value for a global function's type
generic_call_returns_projection a generic function returning its parameter's associated type (`Option<I::Item>`, `I::Item`), called with a concrete argument, has the type the argument's impl binds, under a plain bound and through a supertrait, where the call kept the projection as its type and was refused (E0200 "expected `Option<i32>`, found `Option<i32>`", "expected `i32`, found `Count::Item`")
projection_param_through_method_and_path a parameter typed by a type parameter's associated type (`d: I::Item`) of a generic method or of a generic function called through a module path (`Gen::take_or(&c, 100)`) takes the type the argument's impl binds, where both were refused as E0214 "expected `I::Item`, found `i32`": the argument was judged against the unreduced projection
variant_argument_for_generic_parameter an enum constructor written as the argument for a parameter naming the callee's own type parameters (`plain_opt(Option::Some(3))` with `d: Option<T>`, ruling 158), and a payload-less variant whose path writes its type arguments (`Option::<Option<i32>>::None`, `Option::None::<i64>`), types itself and infers the callee's parameters, where the baseline gave each the callee's unsubstituted parameter type and stopped with E0900 "call to `Some` ... reached codegen with no resolved function"
import_alias_path_sub_module a path continues through a module alias into the module's sub-modules (`J::Inner::deep()` with `import Json as J;`), at any depth and for types, statics, struct literals and enum variants, and a sub-module a path names through an import's binding is loaded although nothing imports it; the alias's module was asked for an exported type `Inner` (E0203 "cannot find type `J::Inner`"), and the sub-module was never loaded
generic_function_value a generic function or a generic owner's method used as a value is one instance, its type arguments from the turbofish or the expected function type - an annotation, a function-typed parameter, `m::f`, `Wrap::<i32>::get`, `Wrap::get` and `Wrap::make`, and inside a generic body - where the baseline typed the value as the template's own signature (E0200 "expected `(i32) -> i32`, found `(T) -> T`") and found no value for a generic owner's method (E0201 "cannot find value `Wrap::get`")
generic_instance_from_use a generic enum's variant or a generic class's construction is the instance its use names - a variant argument the instance its parameter has once the call is bound, a variant call's written type arguments, a class constructed by value with written type arguments or an expected type - where the baseline refused the variant calls as E0238 "expected `T`, found `E`", typed the class construction as the template (E0358 "no method named `get`"), and failed `first_ok(Result::Ok(4), 9)` in code generation (E0600)
global_initializer_at_start a module-level global whose initializer no constant fold answers holds the value it computes, computed before `main` in build order, and a module-level constant of function type is called as a local is, where the baseline refused each such call as E0202 "cannot find function" (and, without them, gave every such global the value 0)
import_plain_path_sub_module a plain import carries reachability into the imported module's sub-modules (`Toml::Sub::three()` with `import IppsmA::Toml;`), at any depth and for types, struct literals, function values and a brace entry's binding, where the baseline loaded the sub-module and refused the path as E0240 "`Toml::Sub` is not reachable from this module"
generic_struct_literal_instance a generic struct's literal written without type arguments is the instance the expected type names - a binding's annotation or a parameter - else the one its field values bind, where the baseline kept the template as the literal's type (E0200 against `Boxy<i32>`; code generation found no field slot, E0638; a generic call taking it was left unbound, E0900)
global_type_from_initializer a module-level variable with no written type (`const n = 5;`, `const k = idf::<i64>;`) takes its initializer's type and is read from a function above it, from `main` and from an importing module, where the baseline never registered it and refused every read (E0201 "cannot find value", E0202 "cannot find function")
closure_keeps_enclosing_parameters a closure checked in a function's body leaves the function's parameters as they were, so after it `return &binding` from a `match` over a pointer parameter is accepted, where the baseline treated the parameter as a body local and refused it (E0455)
variant_payload_binds_call a variant passed to a generic function binds the parameters its payload carries (`err_or(Result::Ok(1), 6000000000)`: `T` from `Ok(1)`, `E` from the literal), where the baseline bound the function's `E` to the enum's own unbound `E` and refused the call (E0200 "expected `i64`, found `E`")
string_octal_escape_is_esc `\033` in a string or character literal is the octal escape for ESC, so `"\033[1m"` is ESC and `[1m`, `\0` alone stays NUL, and an escape ends after three digits or at a non-octal one, where the baseline refused `\0` followed by a digit (E0013)
static_match_arm_field_is_arm_type inside a `static match (T)` arm a field declared `T` is the arm's type, so `widen(this.value)` in the `i64` arm passes an `i64`, where the baseline read the field as `T` and refused the argument (E0214 "expected `i64`, found `T`")
generic_body_own_method_turbofish inside `Box<T>`'s own body `this.map::<i64>(g)` is a `Box<i64>`, the method's own parameter bound by the written argument, where the baseline typed it `Box<U>` and refused the binding (E0200)
module_main_is_an_ordinary_function only the entry file's `main` is the program's entry point, so a sub-module's own `main` is an ordinary function called by its path, where the baseline emitted both as the C entry point and the link refused two definitions of `main` (E0900)
constant_expression_argument_adopts_parameter an argument made only of integer literals adopts the parameter's type as a single literal does when every value it computes fits, so `take_u32(8 * 10000 + 64 * 100)` binds a `u32`, where the baseline kept the expression at `i32` and refused it (E0214, a sign reinterpretation or a narrowing)
type_declared_after_same_named_function a type declared after a function of its name is bound in its module scope as a second binding of the name, as a function after a type is, where the type went missing from the scope and its use was E0203
generic_trait_implemented_twice_through_bound one type implementing a generic trait at two arguments, called through a bound naming one, is answered by the implementation whose head writes the bound's argument and the two methods link as two symbols, where the baseline left the call unbound (E0900 in each copy)
index_and_deref_answered_through_their_trait `a[i]` and a field read through a `Deref` type call the trait's method beside an ordinary method of the same name on the type, where the baseline checked `g[2 as u64]`'s argument against the ordinary `index(string)` (E0214) and called `w.x` ambiguous between the two `deref`s (E0156)
string_plus_beside_own_append `a + b` on two strings concatenates through the standard library's `append` beside a program's own `append` on `string` taking another type, where the baseline's code generation found two `append`s by name (E0900 "`string::append` names several functions")
variant_owner_type_arguments a generic enum's variant constructed with the type arguments written on the enum, `Option::<i32>::Some(4)` and `Result::<i32, string>::Ok(7)`, is that instance's variant, where the baseline found no such variant (E0233 "cannot find `Option::Some`")
compiler_namespace_is_ordinary a program in `namespace compiler::tools` with a table keyed by text is checked like any other and builds, where the baseline refused the field (E0157, a lint meant for the compiler's own modules reaching the program by its path)
overloaded_generic_function_value a function taken as a value whose overloads include a generic one is the overload the turbofish and the expected function type select, where the baseline took the first-declared overload whatever was expected (E0200 "found `(i32) -> i32`") and could not infer it from a two-parameter expected type (E0307)
function_value_arrays arrays of function values, by an alias and as `((i32) -> i32)[]`, a pointer to a function value, and a method whose return type is a function, build and run, where the baseline could not parse a suffix after a parenthesized type (E0100) and emitted any call of a method returning a function as a call through a field (E0622 "carries no field pin")
generic_method_value a method with type parameters of its own taken as a value, `Box::wrap::<i32>` or bound by the expected function type, is one instance of it, where the baseline typed it as the uninstantiated signature (E0200 "found `(T) -> T`")
generic_owner_method_value a generic type's method with type parameters of its own taken as a value, `Wrap::<i32>::conv::<u8>`, is one instance of each, the type's arguments written on the path or bound by the expected type, where the baseline typed the value as the owner type (E0200 "found `Wrap<i32>`")
generic_owner_generic_method_call a call through a path to a generic type's method with type parameters of its own, `Wrap::<i32>::conv::<u8>(7)` or `Wrap::<i32>::keep::<u8>(&w, 1)`, is bound to the method's instance on the type's specialization wherever the method is declared, where the baseline left the call unbound (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved function")
generic_method_on_owner_minted_in_copy a generic type's method with type parameters of its own, called on an owner a generic function's copy is the first to need, member or path, is bound once the owner is made, and an owner the method's own instance first needs is made and bound too, where the baseline left each call unbound (E0900)
alias_path_statics a path through a type alias names what the same path through its target names, `type PI = Pl<i32>; PI::plain(8)` with the target's type arguments, where the baseline found no such static (E0233)
turbofish_in_generic_body a generic owner's method called with its own type arguments inside a generic function, `w.conv::<u32>(5)` on a `Wrap<A>`, returns in them when the method is declared in an `implement` block, where the baseline typed the call as the method's unsubstituted parameter (E0200)
generic_owner_this_param a generic owner's method with a parameter typed `&This` binds an instance's own type as its argument, and one returning `This` returns the instance, where the baseline read `This` as the bare template, found no method (E0358) and refused the return (E0200)
overloaded_generic_method_value a method taken as a value whose overloads include a generic one is the overload the turbofish and the expected function type choose, where the baseline took the first overload and refused a binding typed as another (E0200), and refused every generic owner's overloaded method value (E0307 or E0200)
overloaded_generic_static_call a call to a static method of a non-generic type whose overloads include generic ones is the overload its arguments select, two generic overloads or a generic one beside a plain one, where the baseline left the call unbound and stopped with an internal error (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved function")
array_type_circumfix an array type written in brackets, `[T]` or `[T; N]`, names the type its postfix spelling `T[]` or `T[N]` names, in every position a type is written, where the baseline refused a `[` in type position as a bracket tuple (E0104)
array_literal_and_index_through_trait an array literal initialises an `Array<T>` in every form, and `xs[i]` on an `Array<T>` goes through the library's `Index` implementations, a generic body's included, where the baseline refused the literal (E0200 mismatched types) and the index (E0200 "cannot be indexed with `[]`")
array_index_out_of_range_panics `xs[i]` on an `Array<T>` past its length panics in the library's `Index` implementation, where the baseline refused the literal and the index (E0200)
index_across_await an `Array<T>` local held across an `await` is indexed, read and written, through `Index` after it, where the baseline left the call's receiver unrewritten and failed LLVM verification ("Operand is null", E0900)
await_hands_array_buffer an `await` handing a future a pointer into a `[T]` local's heap buffer (`buf.as_ptr()`) is accepted, the buffer not being poll-frame storage, where the baseline took the `[T]` (now `Array<T>`) for frame storage and refused it as a dangling address (E0455)
async_return_in_scope_forms a `return` inside an `unsafe` block or a `static match` arm of an async function completes the future, releasing what it owns, and a local read there after a suspend is carried, where the baseline left those statements unlowered and refused the program ("must return on every path", E0600; "expected `Poll<i64>`, found `i64`", E0200)
location_reports_call_site `location()` evaluates to the file, line, column and qualified function of its call, or in a `![caller_location]` body to its caller's, where the baseline lowered it as a call to an undefined symbol and the link failed (E0900)
alias_function_type_call a parameter typed by an alias of a function type (in its module or another) is called as that function type, where the baseline resolved the signature before the alias's target was recorded and refused the call (E0213 "expected function, found `Step`")
alias_return_operator a call returning an alias, and a parameter typed by one, take the operators of the aliased type, where the baseline kept the alias type in the signature and refused the operator (E0229 "Cannot apply '+' to TypeAlias and Int")
generic_call_infers_from_array_literal a generic call whose `T` only an array literal argument fixes binds it from the literal's elements and passes the literal as an `Array`, where the baseline typed the literal as a fixed-size array no `[T]` parameter takes and left the call unselected (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved function", or E0214 "expected `[boolean]`, found `[boolean; 3]`" when another argument bound `T`)
fixed_array_rvalue_index a fixed-size array a call returns is indexed through a temporary it is stored to, `pair()[1]` and `triple(10)[i]`, where the element was addressed from the array's value and the module failed LLVM verification (E0900 "GEP base pointer is not a vector or a vector of pointers")
fixed_array_reference_through_function_value a by-value argument in a `&T` parameter of a function value is passed by address, as at a direct call - an `Array<[i32; 2]>`, whose iterator `find`/`filter` predicates take `&Item`, and calls through `(&[i32; 2]) -> boolean` values - where the baseline passed the fixed-size array by value and the module failed LLVM verification (E0900 "Call parameter type does not match function signature!"); its `[string]` `find` passed the string where its address belongs and crashed at run time
this_member_in_every_self_body `This::member` in a generic struct's own body and in a trait impl, generic or not, names the enclosing type as it does in a non-generic struct's body, and a generic struct's static method returning `This` is instantiated, where the baseline refused the trait-impl calls (E0203 "cannot find type `This` in this scope") and any instantiated static `-> This` of a generic struct (E0203 "`This` used outside a trait declaration or impl block", no span)
literal_array_adopts_type_parameter an array literal of numeric literals passed for `[T]` or `[T; N]` takes the `T` another argument (`i64`, `f32`, `u8`, a negative `i64`) or the expected type binds, where the baseline bound `T` to the literals' default first and refused the other argument (E0214 "conflicting types for the type parameter") or the array (E0214 "expected `[u8; 3]`, found `[i32; 3]`")
this_member_in_trait_default `This::member` in a trait's own default body names the trait's member, and each implementation's copy - a struct's, a primitive's, a generic struct's, one overriding a default the copy calls, and a generic trait's - calls the implementing type's, where the baseline refused every such path (E0203 "cannot find type `This` in this scope")
generic_struct_allocate_instance `new` of a generic struct implementing `Allocate` calls each instance's `allocate` and `release`, with the arguments written and with them bound by the expected type or the field values, where the baseline referenced the template's `allocate`, which nothing defines, and failed to link (E0900 "linker invocation failed"), and refused the field-bound `new Cell { v: wide }` (E0200 "expected `i64`, found `T`")
new_generic_enum_variant `new Option<i64>::Some(41)` allocates the instance and builds its payload, where the baseline built the template's variant and refused it (E0600 "payload type of enum variant ... is unresolved")
unit_value_is_the_empty_tuple `()` is the unit value of type `()`, so `return ();` in a `-> ()` function and `()` bound to a `()` global or local compile, where the baseline typed `()` as `void*` and refused them (E0200)
trait_object_type_layout `virtual &Shape`, `virtual mut &Shape`, `virtual Shape*` and `virtual &Conv<i64>` are types of two words (16 bytes, 8-aligned) in parameters, arrays and a struct field, where the baseline did not parse `virtual` in a type (E0104 "expected type, found 'virtual'")
trait_object_conversion a reference or pointer becomes a trait object at an initializer, an assignment, an argument, a return, a struct-literal field, an array element and a variant payload, with the table defined in the implementation's module, and a `virtual T*` compares with `null`, where the baseline refused every conversion as a type mismatch (E0200, E0214)
trait_object_dispatch a call through a trait object reaches each implementation through its table: two implementations behind one object type, a trait default, two traits declaring the same method, a `virtual mut &` receiver, a raw object, a three-word result, a generic body and an async body holding the object across `await`, with the traits, the implementations and the calls in three modules, where the baseline refused every call through an object (E0358 "not supported yet")
trait_object_supertraits a subtrait object calls its supertraits' methods, and theirs, through its own table, which holds each supertrait's methods first and begins with its first supertrait's whole table, the supertrait implementations in another module, where the baseline refused every supertrait method through an object (E0358 "a supertrait's method is not callable through a trait object yet")
trait_object_through_reference a method call through a reference or a pointer to a trait object, at one level or two, `mut` methods and a supertrait's method included, loads the object and calls through its table, where the baseline refused every such call (E0358 "a call through a reference or pointer to a trait object is not supported yet")
trait_object_trait_arguments objects of traits with arguments bind the trait's parameters and associated types positionally and call through their tables with them put in - a generic trait at two arguments, a subtrait's argument flowing into its supertrait, associated types in the body and the head, defaults, a generic function inferring through an object, the standard library's `Chars` through `virtual mut &Iterator<u32>` - where the baseline refused them (E0315 "which takes type arguments", E0314 "its return type names `This`", E0214)
trait_object_satisfies_trait an object satisfies a bound of its own trait and of its supertraits in each form: a generic struct and generic functions instantiated at objects call through the table, reaching two implementations and an override of a default, a projection on an object reads its argument, an implementation bounded on a supertrait applies to a struct of an object, and a growable array of objects builds, where the baseline refused every such bound (E0306) and every growable array of objects (E0900 at `drop_in_place`)
function_value_in_generic_body a function named as a value in a generic body - by its bare name, its module path, a static method's path, bound to a local, passed to a function-typed parameter, inside a generic method, and passed to `filter` on a receiver known only by its bound - is the declaration it names in every copy, where the baseline emitted a null function (E0900 "LLVM module verification failed", "Operand is null")
iterator_generic_default_on_bound a trait default with a type parameter of its own (`map`, `fold`) called on a receiver known only by its bound binds that parameter from an argument whose type names the associated type the bound writes - through a function's bound and an implement block's, with `B` the item type and not - where the baseline left the call unbound (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved method")
iterator_chained_adaptors_on_bound a trait default chained after `filter` on a receiver known only by its bound (`it.filter(f).map(g).count()`, through a function's bound and a method's) reads the adaptor's item as its source's, which the bound answers, binds `map`'s `B` from it and types the call after it, where the baseline left `map` and the call after it unbound (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved method")
iterator_default_through_object a trait default the object's table cannot hold (`map`, `filter`, `fold`, `take`, a `for` loop over `map`) called through `virtual mut &Iterator<i32>` in a generic function and a generic struct's method runs the trait's default compiled once for the object, from two modules, and a type's own `fold` is reached directly and under a bound but not through the object, where the baseline refused the object as the bound (E0306 at each generic function, E0358 at the struct's method, "is not satisfied")
iterator_adaptors_after_take_and_map_on_bound an adaptor chained after `take` or after `map` on a receiver known only by its bound (`it.take(3).map(f).count()`, `it.map(f).filter(p).count()`, a `for` loop over `take(4).map(f).filter(p).map(g)`, and the same chain in a generic struct's method) reads `TakeIter`'s item from its where-clause through the parameter's bound, and types and binds `filter` on a `MapIter` not yet minted, where the baseline left `map` after `take`, `filter` after `map`, and the calls after them unbound (E0900 "reached codegen with no resolved method")
type_constant_struct_body a struct and a union declare constants in their bodies, reached as `Point::ORIGIN`, as `This::DIMENSIONS` in an initializer and as an array length, where the baseline refused `const` in a type body (E0101)
type_constant_implement_blocks inherent `implement` blocks declare constants on a struct, an enum and `i32`, reached through the type and an alias of it, where the baseline read `const` there as a method named `const` (E0100)
type_constant_cross_module a type's constants are read from another module, as a value and an array length, apart from a module global of the same name, where the baseline refused `const` in a type body (E0101)
constant_fold_full_64_bit_range a compile-time integer above `i64::MAX` sizes an array and passes a `static_assert`, where the baseline's folder stopped at `i64::MAX` and refused it (E0239, E0237)
constant_wraps_to_declared_type a constant whose initializer leaves its declared type's range folds to the value wrapped to that type, the value the program reads at run time, and a cast to `char` folds as a 32-bit wrap, where the baseline folded the unwrapped value (`const A: u8 = B + 200` sized `[u8; 300]`, E0237 "static assertion failed") and did not fold the cast (E0237 "not a compile-time constant")
constant_fold_full_128_bit_range a u128 constant above i128::MAX, and arithmetic or a cast crossing i128::MAX, folds, where the baseline's folder stopped at i128::MAX (E0237 "not a compile-time constant")
visibility_internal_within_package `internal` items and members - a function, a constant, a type with a field, a method and a static - reached from another module of the same package, and a dependency's internal items from its own modules, where the baseline did not know the modifier (E0100)
destructure_generic_instance a destructure of a generic struct's instance outside a generic body, `const { hidden: h, shown: s }: Cell<i32> = ...`, binds each field at the instance's argument types, where the baseline refused it as a non-struct (E0361) and typed each binding `void` (E0229)
module_forms a sub-module is declared `module x;`, `internal module x;`, or grouped as `module { a; b; }` and `internal module { c; }`, where only `public module x;` was a declaration and each of these was a parse error (E0100)
fstring_builders_by_identity an f-string's builder calls name their language items, so a module's own functions spelled as the builders neither answer them nor stand in their way, where the baseline bound the calls to the module's functions and refused them (E0214, E0215, E0200)
spaceship_names_ord_compare `a <=> b` on a type with an inherent `compare` beside its `Ord` implementation compares through `Ord::compare`, directly and through an `Ord`-bounded parameter, where the baseline refused the comparison as ambiguous between the two (E0156)
import_brace_binds_module a brace import binds its module as the plain import does, so a path through it loads the sub-module it names, where the baseline did not load it (E0203 "cannot find type `Toml::Sub`")
call_arguments_checked_at_every_callee a variant's arguments convert to a trait-object payload however its instance is named, and a pointer is borrowed for a reference-to-pointer parameter, where the baseline refused a path-named variant's object argument and the pointer (E0214); the arguments that did compile were never converted, and the program crashed in the first call through the object
trait_object_generic_implementation a value whose type implements the trait by a generic implementation, or by one written for an instantiation, converts to a trait object at its instantiation, the standard library's `String` as a `FmtWrite` among them, where the baseline refused every such conversion (E0315 "implements `Sink` by a generic implementation")
method_object_argument a method's trait-object parameter converts its argument, on a struct, an array, an instantiation whose parameter is the object and a trait's implementation, where the baseline found no method of the name (E0358)
all_default_generic_other_arguments a generic type whose every parameter has a default, instantiated with other arguments (`Tally<Double>`, `String<Counting>`), has its own methods, the methods of a trait implemented for every instantiation and its destructor, where the baseline typed each `&this` receiver as the defaults' instantiation and refused every call (E0358 "no method named `bump`", E0213 at `length()`)
native_heap_as_collection_allocator a `String<NativeHeap>` is grown, compared, searched, truncated and shrunk on the native heap, where the baseline found none of `String`'s methods on it (E0358 "no method named `push_byte`", E0213 at `length()`)
extern_public_block_and_function `public extern "C" { ... }` and a `public function` inside an `extern` block are parsed, the block's keyword the visibility of its functions, where the baseline refused both (E0100 "expected ';', found 'C'", E0101 "unexpected token 'public'")
try_converts_error_through_from a `?` in a generic function converts its error through the function's `where F: From<E>` bound, in a plain and an async function, where the baseline left each such `?` unlowered and refused it in codegen (E0600 "`?` operator was not lowered by semantic analysis")
where_bound_on_concrete_type a `where` bound written on a named type or an instantiation directs paths, `?` and method calls in the body to each instantiation's own implementation, where the baseline refused `Wrapper<T>:` as a bound subject with E0100 and gave a bound on a named type nothing
trait_object_from_type_parameter a value of a type parameter bounded by a trait, `This` in a default of the trait, and the receiver of a generic implementation of it convert to an object of the trait, each copy taking its own type's table, where the baseline refused all five such conversions (E0315 "`S` is a type parameter, whose implementation of `Shout` is not known here")
constant_patterns_compare a name in a pattern naming a constant compares the subject against it wherever the constant is declared, and a module path to a constant is a constant pattern, where the baseline stopped on the path patterns with E0900 and bound the subject to an imported constant's name
inherent_method_outranks_trait a type's own method outranks a trait's method of the same name in a method call, a path and a method value, where the baseline refused every such call as an inherent-and-trait tie (E0156)
where_bound_own_method_first under a `where` bound on a type, the type's own `from` outranks the bound's and `(From<E> for HighError)::from(e)` reaches each instantiation's implementation, where the baseline refused the non-generic calls as an inherent-and-trait tie (E0156), and in the generic bodies called the bound's `from` over the type's own and missed the trait's implementation through the impl-qualified path
where_bound_on_concrete_type_declarations a `where` bound on a type, written on a type declaration or an implement block, is an assumption in its methods and a condition on the implementation applying, where the baseline never applied such an implementation and refused every use of one (E0306)
type_path_patterns_compare a payload-less path in a pattern headed by a type means what it means as a value, so `u32::MAX`, `Limits::TOP` and an enum's own constant are compared against and a variant stays a variant, where the baseline refused a primitive head as no pattern (E0113 parse errors) and read every other such path as an enum variant
